lantern-pr 1
# 63
#title Build and publish the Squirrel installer in the release workflow
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/63
#branch feat/release-windows-installer
#base feat/windows-installer
#opened 2026-11-18
#head 691f4434478b51c10278c627cb1f9e3e9c9863ad
#describe what A v* tag now builds the Squirrel installer on Windows and publishes Lantern-Setup.exe, RELEASES and the full nupkg next to the portable zip; SHA256SUMS covers the installer.
#describe before Release assets were the zips and SHA256SUMS only.
#describe after Release assets also hold the installer, RELEASES and the full nupkg; SHA256SUMS lists the four zips and the installer.
#describe verified pnpm run typecheck, release-workflow and workflow-hygiene tests green; the workflow itself was not run.
#plan windows-squirrel-installer s4.2
~ .github/workflows/release.yml
~ scripts/release-checksums.sh
~ test/release-workflow.test.ts
#order test/release-workflow.test.ts
#order .github/workflows/release.yml
#order scripts/release-checksums.sh
#reason .github/workflows/release.yml The Squirrel update feed needs the installer, RELEASES and the nupkg as release assets, so the Windows job now builds and uploads them.
#reason scripts/release-checksums.sh Users download the installer, so SHA256SUMS must cover it and the release must fail when it is missing.
#reason test/release-workflow.test.ts Pins the installer step, its upload and the Setup.exe checksum so a tag cannot release without the installer.
#story A release ships a Windows installer
#step actor A maintainer pushing a v* tag
#step action gets the Windows installer built and published
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#step subject the release assets and their checksums
#file scripts/release-checksums.sh
#file test/release-workflow.test.ts
#below interaction Download an installer, RELEASES and the full package
#below consequence Windows got only a portable zip => Windows also gets an installer, listed in SHA256SUMS
